Addition and scalar multiplication are carried out in the usual way, e.g. if p(x) = x2 + 2x − 1 and q(x) = x3, then 3p(x) + 5q(x) = 5x3 + 3x2 + 6x − 3, which is another polynomial. As an aside, for future examples note that functions like p(x) = (x − 1)(x + 1) + x2(x3 − 5) are still polynomials even though they are not explicitly written in the form above.
