The infinitude and density of the real numbers R can cause pernicious bugs while implementing numerical algorithms. While the theory of error analysis introduced in §1.2 eventually will help us put guarantees on the quality of numerical techniques introduced in future chapters, it is worth noting before we proceed a number of common mistakes and “gotchas” that pervade implementations of numerical methods. We purposefully introduced the largest offender early in §1.1, which we repeat in a larger font
