4.5 Reduced QR Factorization
We conclude our discussion by returning to the most general case A~x ≈ ~b when A ∈ Rm×n is not square. Notice that both algorithms we have discussed in this chapter can factor non-square matrices A into products QR, but the output is somewhat different:
