Proof. Take any vector ~x ∈ Rn\{~0}. The set {~x, A~x, A2~x, · · · , An~x} must be linearly dependent because it contains n + 1 vectors in n dimensions. So, there exist constants c0, . . . , cn ∈ R with cn 6= 0 such that
~0 = c0~x + c1 A~x + · · · + cn An~x.
We can write down a polynomial
